                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game works fine on the Meta Quest 3 using Virtual Desktop. No problems with getting my motion controllers recognized. So I don't know what the negative reviews are going on about. However, this isn't really a good game. It may be worth it at $3.74 USD. However, it definitely isn't worth $14.99 USD.\n\nGame has been in Early Access for over 10 years. The last update was in August of 2016. It shows in the gameplay. I was randomly going up. Picking up weapons was haphazard. Climbing was finnicky. It feels like an Early Access game, but it's been abandoned. \n\nIt should be de-listed. It's a shame because the game had potential if it had ever been polished. The photogrammetry was ahead of its time. It's room-scale, but it does have arm-swing locomotion but it rarely worked correctly. No smooth or snap turning, you have to turn IRL.\n\nRate 4/10. Abandoned, left in a state that it's barely functional. I cannot recommend at full price. Maybe worth it at sale price if you want to know what 2016 VR games were like.",
